## 3. ARCHITECT_TRUST_ANCHOR.asc
```
-----BEGIN PGP PUBLIC KEY BLOCK-----
Comment: PLACEHOLDER - Replace with actual PGP key
Comment: This represents H_genesis in the V6.0 framework
Comment: H = H_genesis (40%) × H_distributed (60%)

[PLACEHOLDER FOR ARCHITECT'S ACTUAL PGP PUBLIC KEY]

To generate your actual key:
1. Install GPG: https://gnupg.org/
2. Generate key: gpg --full-generate-key
3. Export public key: gpg --armor --export your@email.com > ARCHITECT_TRUST_ANCHOR.asc
4. Replace this placeholder with your actual public key

IMPORTANT NOTES:

1. H_genesis represents the immutable origin anchor
2. This key should be generated on an air-gapped system
3. Keep the private key extremely secure
4. Consider key escrow for business continuity
5. Publish key fingerprint through multiple independent channels

VERIFICATION:
Anyone can verify documents signed with this key using:
gpg --verify document.sig document

For V6.0 implementation:
- All major framework changes should be signed with this key
- Guardian Network validates signatures
- H_genesis = 1.0 if signature valid, 0.0 otherwise

-----END PGP PUBLIC KEY BLOCK-----

================================================================================

INSTRUCTIONS FOR RAFA:

1. Generate your PGP key pair
2. Replace this entire file with your exported public key
3. Keep private key secure (offline, encrypted)
4. Sign the first commit of this repository
5. Publish fingerprint on multiple channels

This creates the cryptographic anchor for H_genesis.

